# Jocke Ohlssons Måleri

Swedish single-page site for a painting company in Töreboda / Skaraborg. Visitor language is Swedish (`lang="sv"`).

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, Tailwind CSS v4. Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` (`@theme`).
- Everyday local server: `npm run dev` → http://localhost:3000
- Cloudflare path: vinext + wrangler (`npm run build:vinext` / `deploy:vinext`). Production URL is `src/lib/siteUrl.ts`.
- For Cloudflare, Workers, Wrangler, or caching work, use the official Cloudflare Cursor plugin skill. Do not paste Cloudflare docs into project rules.

## Where things live

- Copy and business facts: `src/lib/content.ts`
- Page composition: `src/app/page.tsx` and `src/components/`
- Project photos: `Photo.tsx` plus pre-resized `public/` srcset variants. Do not send those photos through the image optimizer.
- Contact form: `src/app/api/contact/route.ts`. SMTP keys are listed in `.env.example`.

The established cream / ink / green palette and Playfair + DM Sans pairing is this site's brief, not generic template chrome to rip out by default. Still reject *new* generic AI-template patterns (SaaS card kits, purple gradients, scattered fade-up, decorative numbered markers). Existing code is evidence, not a freeze — better implementations are allowed when the task justifies them.

## Skill routing

- Copy, typo, rename, small non-visual values, unrelated bugs: edit directly. Do not load design, audit, or browser skills.
- New UI or a substantial redesign: `frontend-design`. Targeted visual / layout / responsive / interaction work: apply it proportionally (no full token-system pass).
- `/site-audit` only when the user asks for an audit, review, critique, or diagnosis.
- `browser-verify` after meaningful UI or interaction changes, or when the user asks to test the site. Skip it for text-only edits.
